<title>JAPAN: Sony Corp shares rebound after profit-taking spell.</title>
<headline>Sony Corp shares rebound after profit-taking spell.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sony Corp shares rebounded in Tuesday morning trade, after taking a beating from rounds of profit taking in recent weeks and from a sharp drop in the benchmark Nikkei average on Monday, brokers said.</p>
<p>As of 0145 GMT, Sony shares were up 220 yen at 8,520.</p>
<p>&quot;There are some brokers who are buying up the shares, which could mean that the rally may be short-lived,&quot; a trader at a second-tier brokerage said.</p>
